
  I. About

    "Modernized Vector" brings you the MediaWiki/Wikipedia 2010 look and feel
    for DokuWiki. It is a mostly optical port of the original MediaWiki "vector" skin.
    It intentionally tracks the legacy Vector 2010 look, not the newer
    MediaWiki Vector 2022 skin.

    Website:     <https://github.com/viasnake/dokuwiki-template-vector>
    Original template page: <https://www.dokuwiki.org/template:vector>
    Original author: ARSAVA <https://dev.arsava.com/>
    Maintainer:  viasnake <https://github.com/viasnake/>
    Contact:     See "IV. Support" and "V. Contact".



  II. Installation and update

    This maintained version targets current stable DokuWiki releases and
    supports PHP 7.4 or newer, matching DokuWiki 2025-05-14b
    "Librarian". DokuWiki master currently requires PHP 8.2 or newer.
    Legacy Internet Explorer workarounds have been removed; the template targets
    current evergreen browsers supported by current DokuWiki.

    The installation works as described [1] on DokuWiki.org. Extract the
    downloaded archive into your DokuWiki's "lib/tpl/" folder, then select
    the template in the Config Manager by adjusting the template option. If you
    install from a GitHub source archive, rename the extracted directory to
    "modernizedvector" so the final path is "lib/tpl/modernizedvector/".

    See the GitHub releases and project documentation for update instructions.

    [1] <https://www.dokuwiki.org/template>

    Maintainer verification before release:
      - Run "git diff --check" to catch whitespace errors.
      - Keep "template.info.txt" date and "VERSION" in sync for release
        detection in DokuWiki Extension Manager.
      - Run "python3 tests/release-metadata.py" when release metadata changes.
      - Keep "deleted.files" updated whenever release cleanup removes files
        that may still exist in installed templates.
      - Keep generated local artifacts such as Python "__pycache__" directories
        and "*.pyc" files out of the release tree.
      - Run "python3 tests/release-tree-policy.py" before packaging a release.
      - When publishing a release, keep template.info.txt and the GitHub release
        metadata consistent so Extension Manager update checks stay correct.
      - Run "php -l" over changed PHP files, ideally with each supported PHP
        version used in CI.
      - Run "python3 tests/php74-compatibility.py" when PHP files change.
      - Run "node --check script.js" and
        "node --check tests/mobile-menu-smoke.js" when JavaScript changes.
      - Run "python3 tests/language-coverage.py" when configuration or
        language files change.
      - Run "python3 tests/rendered-html-smoke.py <rendered-html> [...]" when
        template markup changes.
      - Run "python3 tests/style-import-coverage.py <dokuwiki-style.ini>
        style.ini" when bundled DokuWiki component styles or style.ini change.
        CI also runs this check against DokuWiki master so upstream component
        style changes are visible before the next stable release.
      - Run "lessc static/mobile.less" with the same replacement variables as
        CI when mobile styles change.
      - Run "bash -n tests/dokuwiki-runtime-smoke.sh" when the runtime smoke
        script changes.
      - Run "tests/dokuwiki-runtime-smoke.sh" against the current stable
        DokuWiki release. CI runs it with PHP 7.4, 8.2, and 8.4. The smoke
        test renders normal pages, core action modes, media detail pages, the
        media manager popup, css.php output, right-to-left language output,
        and the mobile menu JavaScript smoke.
        The JavaScript smoke needs jsdom and jquery in Node's module path; CI
        installs them into "/tmp/vector-js-smoke". For local runs you can do
        the same and call the script with
        "NODE_PATH=/tmp/vector-js-smoke/node_modules". Set "PHP_BIN" to choose
        a PHP binary and "SMOKE_PORT" or "SMOKE_WORKDIR" when the defaults
        conflict with your environment. Set "VECTOR_SKIP_JS_SMOKE=1" only when
        you intentionally want to run the PHP/runtime checks without the mobile
        menu JavaScript smoke. The smoke script can also download DokuWiki
        branch archives for exploratory future-version checks, for example
        "DOKUWIKI_REF_TYPE=heads DOKUWIKI_TAG=master" with a PHP version
        supported by that branch. The CI workflow can be run manually with the
        same ref type, ref name, and PHP version inputs for exploratory checks.

    Compatibility policy:
      - Prefer current DokuWiki template APIs such as tpl_incdir(),
        tpl_basedir(), tpl_includeFile(), tpl_metaheaders(), tpl_content(),
        and tpl_getMediaFile().
      - Do not reintroduce deprecated DOKU_TPLINC or DOKU_TPL usage.
      - Do not reintroduce legacy Internet Explorer conditionals, HTC
        behaviors, or CSS hacks.
      - Treat PHP files in "modernizedvector/user" as trusted administrator-provided
        configuration, and validate template-managed scalar values before
        emitting HTML attributes.



  III. Customizing the template

    In order to make updates of your installed "modernizedvector" template easy,
    follow these hints for customizing the template:

    - Place your files in "modernizedvector/user"
      The place to store *all* user-defined, custom stuff is the "modernizedvector/user"
      directory because your files will not be touched or overwritten on
      template updates! So you normally can copy all new files into "modernizedvector/"
      to update the template without losing your changes.
      Note: There are example files helping you modify the template.
            They are delivered with the ".dist" extensions. Just remove the
            ".dist" extension to use them.

    - Template include hooks
      DokuWiki include hooks are supported through tpl_includeFile(). For
      upgrade-safe site-local markup, place optional files in your DokuWiki
      "conf" directory or in "lib/tpl/modernizedvector". Supported hook file names are
      "meta.html", "topheader.html", "header.html", "pageheader.html",
      "pagefooter.html", "sidebarheader.html", "sidebarfooter.html", and
      "footer.html".

    - Own logo
      If you want to replace the default logo showed in the upper left, simply
      create a "logo.[svg|png|gif|jpg]" in "modernizedvector/user". The template
      recognizes the file automatically and will use it instead of the default
      logo. If no "modernizedvector/user" logo exists, it also recognizes DokuWiki
      media files at ":wiki:logo.[svg|png|gif|jpg]" and
      ":logo.[svg|png|gif|jpg]".
      Note: Do not forget to empty your browser's cache if you cannot see any
            effect.

    - Own favicon
      If you want to replace the default favicon, create a
      "favicon.[svg|png|ico]" in "modernizedvector/user". The template recognizes the
      file automatically and will use it instead of the default one. If no
      "modernizedvector/user" icon exists, the template also recognizes DokuWiki media
      files at ":wiki:favicon.[svg|png|ico]" and ":favicon.[svg|png|ico]". You
      might find the online FavIcon Generator [1] useful.

    - Own CSS
      To apply additional CSS rules, create a
        - "modernizedvector/user/screen.css" file to influence the normal layout. You
          can rename the "screen.css.dist" to "screen.css" as starting point.
        - "modernizedvector/user/print.css" file to influence the print layout. You
          can rename the "print.css.dist" to "print.css" as starting point.
        - "modernizedvector/user/rtl.css" file to influence right-to-left languages
          like Hebrew. It is loaded only when DokuWiki marks the current
          language direction as right-to-left. You can rename the "rtl.css.dist"
          to "rtl.css" as starting point.
      The file(s) will be included automatically (as the last ones for the
      relevant media after the bundled template styles, therefore you are able
      to override existing styles).
      Note: Do not forget to empty your browser's cache if you cannot see any
            effect.

    - Own JavaScript
      To load additional JavaScript, create a "modernizedvector/user/user.js" file. You
      can rename the "user.js.dist" to "user.js" as starting point (it contains
      some examples and useful comments how to define your own JavaScript).
      When DokuWiki's "defer_js" option is enabled, this file is loaded with
      "defer" as well so it keeps the same execution order as DokuWiki's own
      JavaScript.
      ATTENTION: You have to activate the template option "vector_loaduserjs"
                 (->"Load 'modernizedvector/user/user.js'?") in the DokuWiki Config
                 Manager!

    - Own CSS, language specific
      To apply additional CSS rules only for a specific language, edit/create
      "vector/lang/<your-language>/style.css". This file will be included
      automatically if DokuWiki runs/shows a page in the language of choice,
      after the bundled template styles and before files in "modernizedvector/user".
      Note: Do not forget to empty your browser's cache if you cannot see any
            effect.

    - Own tabs
      To apply own tabs, create a "modernizedvector/user/tabs.php" file. You can rename
      the "tabs.php.dist" to "tabs.php" as a good starting point (it contains
      some examples and useful comments how to define your own tabs). If you
      still have questions after playing with the examples, see "IV. Support"
      on how to get help.

    - Own footer buttons
      To apply own buttons/graphics in the footer (-> these small 80x15 pics),
      create a "modernizedvector/user/buttons.php" file. You can rename the
      "buttons.php.dist" to "buttons.php" as a good starting point (it contains
      some examples and useful comments how to define your own buttons). If you
      still have questions after playing with the examples, see "IV. Support"
      on how to get help.

    - Own boxes
      To apply own boxes in the left column/sidebar, create a
      "modernizedvector/user/boxes.php" file. You can rename the "boxes.php.dist" to
      "boxes.php" as a good starting point (it contains some examples and useful
      comments how to define your own boxes). If you still have questions after
      playing with the examples, see "IV. Support" on how to get help.

    - Security note for user PHP files
      The files in "modernizedvector/user/*.php" are trusted administrator-provided PHP
      snippets. Do not copy untrusted user input into them. For tabs and footer
      buttons, keep element IDs, labels, URLs, image paths, CSS classes,
      access keys, widths, and heights as simple scalar values; malformed
      values are ignored by the template.

    - Web analytics software (Matomo, Google Analytics etc.)
      Tools like Matomo and Google Analytics normally provide a small code
      snippet ("tag") which you have to include on your website to make
      everything work. If you want to use such software with this template,
      create a "modernizedvector/user/tracker.php". This gives the snippet a
      dedicated place, and the template loads it automatically. You can
      rename the "tracker.php.dist" to "tracker.php" as a good starting point
      (it contains a short example and useful comments for adding your own
      tracking code). Keep this file writable only by trusted administrators;
      its content is emitted as raw PHP/HTML.

    - QR code box
      The QR code box uses an external QR code service and sends the current
      page URL to that service. It is disabled by default; enable the
      "vector_qrcodebox" option only when this is acceptable for your wiki.

    - Own Apple Touch Icon
      If you want to replace the default Apple Touch Icon, create an
      "apple-touch-icon.png" in "modernizedvector/user". If no "modernizedvector/user" icon exists,
      the template also recognizes DokuWiki media files at
      ":wiki:apple-touch-icon.png" and ":apple-touch-icon.png". Have a look at
      Apple's developer database (cf. "Configuring Web Applications" [2]) if you
      need more information.

    [1] <https://tools.dynamicdrive.com/favicon/>
    [2] <https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/AppleApplications/Reference/SafariWebContent/ConfiguringWebApplications/ConfiguringWebApplications.html>



  IV. Support

    If you need help, check the FAQ [1] and try to find useful information by
    using the DokuWiki Search page [2]. If you found nothing helpful, ask your
    question at the DokuWiki forum [3] (preferred) or IRC channel [4].

    [1] <https://www.dokuwiki.org/template:vector#faq>
    [2] <https://www.dokuwiki.org/?do=search>
    [3] <https://forum.dokuwiki.org/>
    [4] <https://www.dokuwiki.org/irc>



  V. Contact

    If you think you have found a bug or have a useful idea (a.k.a. "feature
    request"), create an issue [1] on GitHub.

    Feel free to submit patches as GitHub pull requests. Please try to respect
    the DokuWiki coding style [2] as this template follows its rules.

    [1] <https://github.com/viasnake/dokuwiki-template-vector/issues>
    [2] <https://www.dokuwiki.org/devel:coding_style>



  VI. Other notes

    This fork is maintained through GitHub issues and pull requests [1]. The
    original ARSAVA project links are kept in the history for attribution, but
    support requests for this fork should use the current project tracker.

    [1] <https://github.com/viasnake/dokuwiki-template-vector/issues>



  VII. Explanatory notes about the dirs of this template

    - "modernizedvector/conf"
      Contains some configuration files (do NOT edit them!), especially
        - default.php: default settings [1]
        - metadata.php: configuration metadata [2]

    - "modernizedvector/lang"
      Language files (subdir names = language code). You may copy the English
      language files and translate them if your language is missing. Submit
      translation updates through GitHub issues or pull requests (cf. "V.
      Contact").

    - "modernizedvector/static"
      Static files (images, CSS, JavaScript). The interesting stuff is located
      in subdirs (as described below).
      - "3rd"
        Static files originally taken from a third party like MediaWiki or
        DokuWiki. The subdir "dokuwiki" contains files originally taken from the
        DokuWiki "default" or "starter" template. The subdir "vector" contains
        files taken from the MediaWiki "vector" skin.
      - "css"
        All non-3rd-party Cascading Style Sheets (CSS). See the linked article [3]
        for more information about how the CSS is handled.
      - "img"
        All non-3rd-party images files.
      - "js"
        All non-3rd-party JavaScript files.

    - "modernizedvector/user"
      Place for user-defined stuff. E.g. if you want to use your own logo,
      copy a logo.[svg|png|gif|jpg] in here. See "III. Customizing the
      template" for details.

    - "modernizedvector/tests"
      Maintainer-facing smoke tests. "dokuwiki-runtime-smoke.sh" installs this
      worktree into a temporary DokuWiki release checkout and checks the main
      template entry points under E_ALL. "mobile-menu-smoke.js" runs the
      template JavaScript against rendered DokuWiki HTML through jsdom and
      jquery, so it can catch mobile menu regressions without a full browser.
      "php74-compatibility.py" flags common PHP 8+ syntax and standard library
      calls while this template declares PHP 7.4 support.
      "release-metadata.py" checks "template.info.txt" and "VERSION" fields
      that DokuWiki Extension Manager consumes.
      "release-tree-policy.py" checks required template entry points, the CI
      workflow, maintainer smoke/policy scripts, "deleted.files", and common
      generated artifact patterns. It also blocks URL helper patterns known to
      cause double-escaped HTML attributes.
      "language-coverage.py" checks that template configuration metadata,
      Config Manager labels, and runtime language keys stay in sync.
      "rendered-html-smoke.py" checks rendered HTML for duplicate IDs, broken
      skip links, double-escaped URL attributes, required content landmarks,
      DokuWiki housekeeping hooks, and language direction metadata.
      "style-import-coverage.py" checks that Vector's bundled DokuWiki
      component styles still cover the component styles listed by the current
      standard DokuWiki template. The tests directory ships with an Apache
      ".htaccess" deny rule because these files are maintainer-facing, not
      template assets. The bundled deny rules use Apache 2.4 "Require all
      denied" with an Apache 2.2 fallback.

    [1] <https://www.dokuwiki.org/devel:configuration#default_settings>
    [2] <https://www.dokuwiki.org/devel:configuration#configuration_metadata>
    [3] <https://blog.andreas-haerter.com/2011/03/16/how-to-create-a-maintainable-dokuwiki-template>



  VIII. Original creation transcript

    These notes document the original template import and are kept for historical context.


    - Downloaded the MediaWiki Vector skin source from
      <https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Skin:Vector>.

    - Installed DokuWiki locally for testing.

    - Copied all "monobook for DokuWiki" sources because it already fit some of
      my needs regarding config options and non-layout features. I used
      the source of the "monobook for DokuWiki" template as base for "vector for
      DokuWiki".

    - Replaced "monobook" with "vector" in:
      - /conf/*
      - /lang/*
      - /detail.php
      - /inc_cite.php
      - /inc_detail.php
      - /main.php
      - /mediamanager.php

    - After investigation, some 3rd-party files were copied into the provided
      places within "/modernizedvector/static/3rd".
      - The following files were copied from the original vector skin:
        - /skins/vector/main-ltr.css
        - /skins/vector/main-rtl.css
        - /skins/vector/images/*
      - The following files were copied from Andreas Gohr's "default" template:
        - /default/*.css (see <https://blog.andreas-haerter.com/2011/03/16/how-to-create-a-maintainable-dokuwiki-template> why I did that)
        - /default/images/closed.gif
        - /default/images/favicon.ico
        - /default/images/open.gif
        - /default/images/tocdot2.gif
      - The following files were copied from Anika Henke's "starter" template:
        - /starter/images/external-link.png
        - /starter/images/unc.png
        - /starter/images/email.png

    - Edited:
      - "/modernizedvector/static/3rd/vector/main-ltr.css"
        "/modernizedvector/static/3rd/vector/main-rtl.css"
        The original image urls were adjusted for this DokuWiki template.
        The LTR file is loaded through DokuWiki's CSS dispatcher; the RTL file
        is loaded directly only for right-to-left languages, so its urls remain
        relative to its own directory.
        To make this clear, a comment was added at the top of the files.

      - "/modernizedvector/static/3rd/dokuwiki/*.css"
        The original image urls were adjusted for this DokuWiki template.
        "url(static/3rd/dokuwiki/").
        To make this clear, a comment was added at the top of the files.

    - Visited <https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=ASCII>, copied the
      HTML source and used Tidy to get a valid, clean, and
      correctly indented base markup (after core removal, for sure). This markup
      was then compared with the current main.php and needed changes were made.

    - Created new files:
      - "vector/static/css/print.css"
      - "vector/static/css/rtl.css"
      - "vector/static/css/screen.css"
      Relevant information is documented in the inline comments.

    - Completed the initial port.

    - After ~1 year, I switched the CSS base from DokuWiki's default template
      to <https://www.dokuwiki.org/template:starter>. I edited some files; see
      "vector/static/3rd/dokuwiki/00_starter-tmpl-notes.txt" for details.
